            <ArticleTitle>Double cardiac pseudoaneurysm in a postoperative patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5543/tkda.2015.06777</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A mitral-aortic intervalvular fibrosa pseudoaneurysm is a rare complication after aortic and mitral valve replacement and aortic root replacement. A left ventricular pseudoaneurysm after mitral valve replacement is also a rare complication. Here, we describe a 48-year-old woman with a history of a Bentall operation and mitral valve replacement 6 years before, presenting with double pseudoaneurysms in the left ventricle and mitral-aortic intervalvular fibrosa, detected via transesophageal echocardiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
